.TH http_response_free 3 "HTTP Library Functions" "QuickJS" "HTTP Library Functions"

.SH NAME
http_response_free \- Free an HTTP response structure

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/http.h>
.B void http_response_free(http_response* r);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B http_response_free function frees an HTTP response structure.

The function takes one parameter:
.I r
The HTTP response structure.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B http_response_free function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/http.h>

int main() {
  // Assume r is a valid HTTP response structure
  http_response r;

  // Initialize r

  // Use the HTTP response

  http_response_free(&r);

  return 0;
}
.!
